course: dictionary
lesson: 5386
title: One word, three meanings: knockout
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: One word can have more than one meaning, so the words around it are your clues. «The knockout stage of the World Cup» is about sport. Teams that lose a game leave the competition, so you can work out that knockout means a competition where losers go out.
explain: In boxing, a knockout is when a fighter is knocked down and cannot get up in time. Maths can give you clues too: «with 16 teams, there are 8 + 4 + 2 + 1 = 15 games». In a knockout contest, every game knocks out exactly one player or team, so the sums must add up to one winner.
explain: Informally, «The show was a knockout» does not mean anyone was hit. It means the show was extremely good. Check by swapping in «extremely good»: if the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Knockout is a noun (a knockout, knockouts) and an adjective (knockout). It can also be written knock-out.
fact: In a knockout competition, the loser of each game leaves, until one winner is left.
fact: With 8 players, you need 4 + 2 + 1 = 7 matches to find one winner.
fact: Informally, a knockout is something or someone extremely good or beautiful.
fact: Useful phrases include knockout round, knockout punch and knock-out blow.
exercise: «In a knockout contest, every match knocks out exactly one player.» What is a knockout competition? | A contest with no losers at all | A game played only on the beach | *A contest where the loser of each game leaves until one winner is left | A contest where everyone wins a prize
exercise: «With 16 teams, there are 8 + 4 + 2 + 1 = 15 games.» How many games are there with 8 teams in a knockout competition? | 15 | 8 | *7 | 4
exercise: «The show was a knockout.» What does knockout mean here? | A show that ended early because of rain | *Something extremely good | A show with no music | A fight in a boxing ring
test: «32 teams went through to the knockouts.» Which word names the later rounds where losers go out? | teams | groups | *knockouts | games
test: In boxing, what is a knockout? | A fight where nobody wins | A point given for good footwork | *A fighter is knocked down and cannot get up in time | Both fighters shake hands at the end
exam: «Eight players need seven matches to find one winner.» In a knockout contest, how many matches are needed for 8 players? | 4 | 6 | *7 | 8
